<title>USA: B&amp;H Ocean Carriers unit sells $125 mln debt.</title>
<headline>B&amp;H Ocean Carriers unit sells $125 mln debt.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following 144a debt issue from Equimar Shipholdings Inc was priced on Friday via lead manager Credit Suisse First Boston Corp, according to market sources.</p>
<p>Equimar Shipholdings Ltd and parent B&amp;H Ocean Carriers Ltd are Liberian corporations.</p>
<p>The issue was increased in size by $25 million.</p>
<p>BORROWER EQUIMAR SHIPHOLDINGS INC</p>
<p>AMT $125 MLN	   COUPON 9.875 PCT  MATURITY 7/1/2007</p>
<p>TYPE 1ST PFD MTG NTS ISS PRICE 100.00  FIRST PAY DATE 1/01/98</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S B3	YIELD 9.875 PCT   PAY FREQ SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P B-PLUS	SPREAD 352 BPS    CALLABLE NON CALL FIVE</p>
<p>NOTES: Guaranteed by B+H Ocean Carriers Ltd.</p>
<p>: Three year equity call for 25 percent at 109.875.</p>
<p>((--U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212-859-1672))</p>
</text>
